    midout: the base-64 kernel's phase 3b on digit-major slices, four chunks per lane
    
    The narrow kernel gets the wide kernel's layout and lane map: slices
    [(v * 16 + q) * 2 + half], lane t covering chunks (t % 16) ^ 4k of one
    list entry (64 entries per cube step), each probe's digits read once
    for four chunks, conflict-free reads, and the W 64 phase-2 stores
    rotated over the four tasks' chunks. F_DROP_REC drops cube 0's
    second-chunk records. Words, masks and records are as before; their
    order in a slab changes.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

